WEBVTT

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:12.570
<b>I tried coming alone to our usual park.</b>

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.070
<b>It's a feeling I've never felt.</b>

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:21.660
<b>Like a child, frightened by the sound of the wind</b>

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.670
<b>I ran back along the path home.</b>

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:33.970
<b>The sky outside the window is too vast. Where are you now?</b>

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.130
<b>Please, may this reach you...</b>

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:44.690
<b>Dear Lord, if you ever grant wishes,</b>

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:50.110
<b>grant my wish right now, please!</b>

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:56.240
<b>I want to hear your voice, I miss you! I want to see you now!</b>

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:00.830
<b>Why must you already be looking toward tomorrow?</b>

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:06.210
<b>Don't just brush it off, saying the time has slipped by.</b>

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.540
<b>Once more...</b>

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:14.550
<b>I love you, and yet it's been too late since long ago.</b>

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:19.140
<b>Even if I give up, it can't be like the past.</b>

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:24.350
<b>Don't just decide so simply there's no way, no choice.</b>

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:28.230
<b>Smile once more.</b>

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:54.710
Why? Why did it turn out like this?

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:59.380
All we wanted to do was 
to protect Center City...

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:04.260
Why...

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:10.430
What? We broke through the checkpoints.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:13.440
They don't know where we're headed.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:17.250
Now all we need to do is head to our 
destination without sticking out.

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:18.900
Exactly!

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:21.450
Although, don't let down your guard.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:25.150
What's with the long face?

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:26.910
No, it's nothing really...

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:30.230
Don't worry, we'll get through this somehow!

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:33.210
I think you're being a 
bit too optimistic there.

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:35.490
Fine, then how should I be?

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:39.950
Our journey is going to 
get rough from now on.

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.860
Even after we escape to my 
friend's place in Nevada...

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:45.380
Are you listening, Joey?

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:48.140
To clear Heroman's name,

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:52.080
all kinds of challenges are 
going to stand in our way.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:57.030
And to get through them, we're 
going to need Heroman's power,

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:59.610
and all the experience you 
have gained to this point.

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:05.760
It goes without saying that we'll need 
Heroman to grow his powers even further.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:09.200
Heroman's powers?

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.510
I'm not saying you need to be 
constantly worried about it.

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:14.240
But, you mustn't relax, ever.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:21.270
Yeah, that's the spirit!

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:24.350
Can't go to battle on 
an empty stomach, right?

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:26.220
First, we have a meal.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:29.070
And we'll stock up while we're at it.

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:30.560
Music to my ears!

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:47.950
The coal mine he ran into is a 
twisted maze of countless tunnels.

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:52.800
It's pointless. He's already 
escaped from Center City.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.450
The question is, where is he heading?

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:59.790
We'll continue with the checkpoints 
on the major roadways.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:02.450
The search is already 
on for Denton's vehicle.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.900
We can also put up in various locations...

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:07.920
All we can do is wait, then.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.220
Until he makes a mistake.

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:12.890
Agent Hughes.

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:14.110
What is it?

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:16.140
Dr. Minami is here to see you.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:40.910
<i>The inclement weather on the east coast 
is affecting more than 20,000 people.</i>

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:43.130
<i>Now, continuing to the next story.</i>

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:46.110
<i>With regards to the battle between 
police and a mysterious power</i>

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:48.640
<i>in the outskirts of Center City 
that happened the other day,</i>

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:55.170
<i>the government believes the probability is 
high that it was a remnant of the Skrugg.</i>

00:04:55.170 --> 00:05:00.250
<i>Although there was some damage from the 
incident, they were successful in driving it away.</i>

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:03.560
<i>It looks like they prevented 
it from entering the city.</i>

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:07.270
What the heck are they 
saying? It was their doing!

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:09.770
Why are they saying that?

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:11.700
Public opinion is important.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:15.590
If they can convince people 
they're fighting "evil,"

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:18.230
then they can fight without holding back.

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:19.860
We're up against the government here.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:22.310
Don't go getting upset 
about every little thing.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:26.670
<i>Now, the next story.</i>

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:30.550
<i>A middle school teacher and 
a student have gone missing.</i>

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:36.690
<i>They have been identified as Center City 
Middle School teacher Mr. Matthew Denton,</i>

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:39.980
<i>and this student, Mr. Joseph Carter Jones.</i>

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:44.900
<i>The police believe they may be 
involved with some incidents,</i>

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:46.930
<i>and have opened up a criminal investigation.</i>

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:50.800
<i>If anyone has any information, please 
contact your local law enforcement department.</i>

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:50.590
Well, that <i>is</i> surprising.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:53.260
They'll even go this far?

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:55.750
And wait, what am I, chopped liver?

00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:58.000
We've got to get out of here, quick.

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:09.840
It looks like we should 
avoid eating out for now.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:13.110
Sheesh, it's like we're wanted men.

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:23.920
Got it? Try not to stand out at all.

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:26.310
We'll get our shopping 
done quickly and smoothly.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:32.850
I may have told you before, but please 
don't place too great a hope on my wallet.

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:46.300
I can't stand it!

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.980
That incident the other 
day was right near here!

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:51.710
Don't worry, the government's handling it.

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:53.570
They'll get 'im soon.

00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:56.260
Some remnant of the Skrugg isn't 
anything to be worried about.

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:59.350
But anyway, what do you 
think that white alien is?

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:02.040
It has such an evil face!

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:03.730
Joey!

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:10.120
Joey...

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:15.280
Let's hurry and finish the shopping.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:17.350
Yeah. Let's do that.

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:20.540
Let's see here...

00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:23.760
Which would be good?

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.320
Something the matter?

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:30.760
No...

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:33.500
I'm going to the bathroom.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:54.740
Hello?

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:56.200
<i>Lina...</i>

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:58.540
Joey? It's you, Joey, right?

00:07:59.390 --> 00:08:00.760
What's happened?

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:03.120
I saw about Heroman on TV...

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:07.950
There were men in black asking 
about you around your house.

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:11.050
And Prof. Denton has gone missing, too!

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:13.250
<i>I'm sorry, a lot has happened.</i>

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:15.090
Anyway, Joey...

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:15.970
Are you okay?

00:08:16.790 --> 00:08:19.710
Yeah! The Professor and Psy are safe as well.

00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:22.450
I wouldn't say we're doing 
super or anything, though...

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:25.200
<i>Is there anything I can do?</i>

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:28.610
Yeah. There's one thing I'd like to ask.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:30.620
<i>What is it? Anything you want!</i>

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:33.910
Don't worry about us.

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:36.030
<i>Joey...</i>

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:40.990
<i>I'll see you again, right?</i>

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:44.830
I have to hang up now.

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:46.590
<i>Joey, Joe-</i>

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:51.210
Phone trace is complete.

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:55.330
4649 North Street, Lukesville.

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:57.470
It's a public phone inside the grocery store.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:59.150
Great, good going.

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:00.880
Use the satellite data!

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:03.600
Determine which one is 
Denton's vehicle immediately!

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.990
When you've found it, track it!

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:08.400
We'll head there immediately.

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.500
Mr. Hughes.

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:13.260
Let me say something first.

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:15.520
We're up against technology 
that is out-of-this-world.

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:18.990
If you continue using these half-hearted 
tactics you will fail again.

00:09:19.310 --> 00:09:20.680
Half-hearted?

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:25.490
It seems to me that you are more interested 
in the humans than the target itself.

00:09:26.010 --> 00:09:28.220
That's because we are up against humans here.

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:30.880
That is how we managed to 
track them down, after all.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:33.510
Well, fine then.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:36.470
But I'll have you remember this:

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:40.450
We are not meant for fighting humans!

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:42.450
Then I'll say something as well:

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:45.520
I am in command here, and don't forget it.

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:57.850
I wonder just how long you'll 
be able to say that, Mr. Hughes.

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:03.700
He's only involved in the investigation because 
of pressure from his connections to the military...

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:17.250
At this pace I think we'll arrive 
faster than I anticipated.

00:10:17.830 --> 00:10:19.850
Faster... Like, how fast?

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:23.250
Including rest, another two days or so.

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:27.600
Professor Denton.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:28.560
What is it?

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:30.870
Something is strange.

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:32.020
Strange?

00:10:35.210 --> 00:10:36.880
We're in a town, but...

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:39.600
...there are no people.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:41.960
You're right.

00:10:42.710 --> 00:10:43.860
It couldn't be...

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:53.890
How'd they find us?

00:10:53.890 --> 00:10:56.200
That's not what's important right now!

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:57.710
What's important is...

00:10:58.310 --> 00:11:00.980
...how we can get through this crisis!

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:04.260
Stop! Stop or we shoot!

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:05.810
Damn it!

00:11:08.380 --> 00:11:09.050
After them!

00:11:09.050 --> 00:11:10.090
Hurry!

00:11:14.890 --> 00:11:16.480
I'll draw them away.

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:17.920
We're counting on you!

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:20.860
Psy, is there some good place to meet up?

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:22.640
There's some warehouses two blocks ahead!

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:23.360
Let's meet behind there!

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:24.900
Got it!

00:11:27.030 --> 00:11:31.040
Heroman... Engage!

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:40.230
It's here!

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:41.870
That's the target?

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:43.300
Prepare to fire!

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:48.460
Heroman... Go!

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:25.630
In the middle of the town...

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:27.030
Heroman!

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:54.330
What are you doing? After him!

00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:05.010
Something that giant, disappeared?

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:10.010
Keisha, the military's on the move!

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:11.610
I've been waiting for this!

00:13:11.610 --> 00:13:13.900
Hurry up, we're leaving immediately!

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:15.220
I know!

00:13:29.150 --> 00:13:30.420
We're back.

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:35.470
Good. We managed to get away 
from them thanks to you.

00:13:35.470 --> 00:13:39.460
So it seems like they haven't got 
us completely surrounded this time.

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:41.300
What do you plan to do?

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:44.550
You expect to escape in such a big vehicle?

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:45.920
I think we can.

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:49.220
But I'll need everyone's help.

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:51.250
Psy, get in the back.

00:13:51.250 --> 00:13:54.030
You want me to cook or something?

00:13:54.550 --> 00:13:58.110
Turn the transceiver in 
the back to channel 7.

00:13:58.110 --> 00:13:59.230
Roger that!

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:02.570
After that, flip the switch on the side.

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:05.380
What's he planning?

00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:07.450
We'll monitor their transmissions!

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:09.300
That'll take the wind out of their sails!

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:10.720
<i>Target has been lost!</i>

00:14:11.270 --> 00:14:12.980
It worked!

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:16.360
<i>I think the vehicle was proceeding north on 3rd!</i>

00:14:16.360 --> 00:14:18.000
<i>Encircle a large perimeter!</i>

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:19.140
<i>Roger.</i>

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:21.100
<i>We'll use the satellite to track them down.</i>

00:14:21.100 --> 00:14:22.450
I won't let you do that.

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:27.260
What's going on?

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:31.450
Why did they ignore my orders to 
stand by and start the plan?

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:38.080
They received an order to start a 
direct attack if they had the chance...

00:14:40.010 --> 00:14:41.860
Is this Minami's doing?

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:45.300
This is a war.

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:49.010
Victory goes to the one who strikes first!

00:14:56.090 --> 00:14:57.470
What's going on?

00:14:57.470 --> 00:14:59.700
We still haven't found the target!

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:01.900
<i>Target has changed to heading east!</i>

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:04.000
<i>It seems like they're heading 
to the highway entrance!</i>

00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:06.960
<i>To repeat: The target is to the east!</i>

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:09.510
Damn it! Move out immediately!

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:10.960
Gotcha!

00:15:11.530 --> 00:15:14.010
Good! All clear over here, too.

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:20.430
I can just imagine their freaked out faces...

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:22.460
What have you done?

00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:25.260
What? Just a little prank.

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:33.500
Now we head to the west which should 
be unguarded, and we're home free!

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:38.800
Really?

00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:40.870
They can do something like that?

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:42.910
What's happened?

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:47.240
It seems that the military satellites and 
transportation systems have been hacked!

00:15:47.240 --> 00:15:48.400
What?

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:53.300
The satellite, tracking system, and 
all security cameras in this area...

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:55.150
We can't operate any of them!

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:57.860
What in the world?

00:15:58.340 --> 00:16:01.400
Where are our units located right now?

00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:04.430
The target was heading east,

00:16:04.430 --> 00:16:07.520
so our forces are spread out around 
the crucial entrance to the highway.

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:11.230
The target's to the west!

00:16:11.230 --> 00:16:13.110
Move our forces immediately!

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:14.670
Y-Yes, sir!

00:16:14.670 --> 00:16:17.140
Use secure channels for communication.

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:18.950
Secure channels?

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:21.750
We're up against someone who 
can hack military satellites.

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:24.120
It'd be an easy matter for them 
to intercept communications.

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:26.180
Hurry! Don't waste any time!

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:27.190
Roger!

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:36.170
All right! We're almost out of the town.

00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:49.140
Stop this futile resistance! 
You have nowhere left to run!

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:53.490
Surrender!

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:58.280
If you surrender, you won't be harmed!

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:04.560
Yeah, like we'd honestly believe that.

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:07.910
I repeat, surrender!

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:14.880
Negotiations have broken down!

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:17.340
Begin the attack!

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:06.170
Where's your friend?

00:18:06.170 --> 00:18:07.240
Friend?

00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:09.910
I dunno... What was I doing again?

00:18:18.960 --> 00:18:21.450
Get outta here, Joey.

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:28.250
<i>What happened?</i>

00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:30.460
<i>We've captured Denton!</i>

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:35.000
<i>But we can't find the boy or the target!</i>

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:37.270
What?!

00:18:38.850 --> 00:18:41.070
Go back! Go back!

00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:44.940
So the Ghost wasn't being 
transported by vehicle?

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:49.040
I don't know, but we haven't found the Ghost!

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:53.410
Land the helicopter. I'm 
getting off on the ground.

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:01.290
That boy will try to avoid fighting.

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:04.640
So in that case, he'd...

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:10.840
Begin questioning him.

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:14.400
Spread out a search party 
focusing on the forest area.

00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:15.300
Got it?

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:16.210
Roger!

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:22.200
Howard...

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:23.330
Yes, sir?

00:19:23.330 --> 00:19:24.470
You're in charge.

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:25.560
Yes?

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:27.090
Then, what about you?

00:19:27.950 --> 00:19:31.890
I'm really not cut out for group operations.

00:19:32.930 --> 00:19:34.660
If anything happens, contact us!

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:37.230
Roger that!

00:19:58.750 --> 00:19:59.980
Are you okay, Psy?

00:19:59.980 --> 00:20:00.890
Yeah...

00:20:00.890 --> 00:20:02.760
...is what I'd like to say, anyway.

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:04.830
But I'm obviously holding you back.

00:20:04.830 --> 00:20:06.110
That's not true!

00:20:06.110 --> 00:20:08.260
I feel a lot more confident with you here!

00:20:10.300 --> 00:20:14.450
It's more important that you get 
away from here than feel safe!

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:16.190
Go on ahead!

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:18.570
No!

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:21.000
I can't leave you behind, Psy!

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:23.140
So you want the two of us to be caught?

00:20:24.330 --> 00:20:25.550
Go!

00:20:25.550 --> 00:20:27.750
As long as you two aren't captured...

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:30.080
The Professor and I will 
handle things somehow!

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:30.970
But!

00:20:30.970 --> 00:20:32.900
Get outta here, Joey!

00:20:32.900 --> 00:20:34.410
For our sakes, as well...

00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:36.920
Psy...

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:38.700
Okay?

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:53.810
Don't worry. I'll buy you plenty of time.

00:21:12.550 --> 00:21:14.190
Now, then...

00:21:14.890 --> 00:21:16.560
Let's rock this place real good.

00:21:17.870 --> 00:21:22.410
It might not work on humans, but it'll 
get their attention, that's for sure!

00:22:02.630 --> 00:22:03.920
I found you.

00:22:29.310 --> 00:22:32.400
<b>I want to get to know you better,</b>

00:22:32.400 --> 00:22:35.490
<b>to go at each other with our true feelings.</b>

00:22:35.490 --> 00:22:41.830
<b>Your tears and smile are both here.</b>

00:22:42.290 --> 00:22:46.260
<b>No matter how hard it is, I won't be scared any more.</b>

00:22:46.260 --> 00:22:49.320
<b>With both of us, we can go anywhere.</b>

00:22:49.320 --> 00:22:54.760
<b>Since you're the one who taught me that I'm not alone.</b>

00:22:54.760 --> 00:23:02.450
<b>Every time I mutter the words "I was born to meet you"</b>

00:23:03.120 --> 00:23:07.490
<b>my unease disappears, and my heart burns stronger.</b>

00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:14.440
<b>Thank you. We'll go on together with a sign only we understand.</b>

00:23:14.880 --> 00:23:19.300
<b>Carve out this irreplaceable time!</b>

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:23.840
<b>I can't move away from here.</b>

00:23:23.840 --> 00:23:28.060
<b>Because I live feeling the same heartbeat.</b>

00:23:28.580 --> 00:23:30.280
<b>I want to protect you to the very last,</b>

00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:32.680
<b>to protect the promise built up.</b>

00:23:33.460 --> 00:23:40.080
<b>Thank you. We'll go on together with a sign only we understand.</b>

00:23:40.300 --> 00:23:45.810
<b>We are carving out this irreplaceable time!</b>

00:23:51.060 --> 00:23:53.490
On the next Heroman:

00:23:53.490 --> 00:23:56.740
Is it really okay for me to trust you?

00:23:56.740 --> 00:24:01.120
Just as he thought he'd escaped, 
he meets NIA Agent Hughes.

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:05.800
But what he says is the opposite 
of what Joey expected.

00:24:05.800 --> 00:24:08.730
With the possibility of talking reopened,

00:24:08.730 --> 00:24:11.880
the situation seems to be heading 
to a peaceful conclusion, when...

00:24:12.190 --> 00:24:15.530
Next time on Heroman #15: Revolt!

00:24:15.910 --> 00:24:18.570
Heroman... Attack!
